## Why This Is Asked
Tests privacy-preserving ML at scale with regulatory constraints, multi-tenant isolation, and production-grade governance. Requires knowledge of Vertex AI Confidential Computing, Dataflow pipelines, Data Catalog/DLP, and automated rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Vertex AI Confidential Computing (VMs/TPUs)
- Dataflow ingestion and residency controls
- Private endpoints and per-tenant budgets
- Data Catalog governance and DLP coverage
- Adversarial robustness testing and dataset/versioning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: basic adversarial test harness
function evalAdversarial(model, sample) {
  const adv = generateAdversarialSample(sample);
  const pred = model.predict(adv);
  return pred.accuracy;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to orchestrate per-hospital rollback across regions?
- How to quantify privacy risk and ensure end-to-end DLP coverage?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design a scalable, compliant, and observable MLOps workflow that supports multi-tenant isolation while meeting real-time processing requirements and governance standards.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant architecture with per-tenant resource isolation
- Real-time stream processing with PII redaction at ingestion
- Feature store management for tenant-specific model training
- Canary deployment strategies for safe model rollouts
- Model explainability and drift detection with automated rollback
- Comprehensive data lineage and governance tracking
- Cost management controls at the tenant level
- Late-arrival data handling within specified time windows

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: canary deployment decision logic
if (tenantDrift[tenant] < DRIFT_THRESHOLD) {
  promoteCanaryToProduction(tenant);
} else {
  rollbackToStableModel(tenant);
  triggerAlert(tenant, 'Model drift detected');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle schema evolution across tenants?
- What strategies would you use for optimizing costs in a multi-tenant environment?
- How would you ensure data consistency when processing late-arriving events?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a candidate's ability to design a compliant, language-agnostic text classification pipeline using Vertex AI, Dataflow, and Pub/Sub, with privacy safeguards and practical operational concerns.

## Key Concepts

- Dataflow-based redaction and translation for multilingual content
- End-to-end data lineage: storage of raw and processed text
- Weekly Vertex AI training with canary deployment
- Drift and latency monitoring with rollback strategy
- Practical cost considerations: storage, translation, training, and serving

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: dataflow-style transform for redaction/translation
function redactAndTranslate(record) {
  const redacted = redactPII(record.text);
  const translated = (record.language !== 'en') ? translate(redacted, 'en') : redacted;
  return { id: record.id, text_en: translated, raw: record.text };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate translation quality across languages in this setup?
- What changes would you make to handle sudden traffic spikes without violating privacy constraints?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-tenant inference with strict data residency, budgets, and auditable lineage in a real-world GCP setup.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation in Vertex AI Endpoints and Feature Store namespaces
- Routing logic with per-tenant budget and latency SLAs
- Data Catalog metadata tagging for lineage and governance
- Drift detection and rollback triggers per tenant

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing function
async function routeRequest(tenantId, req) {
  const budgetOk = checkBudget(tenantId);
  const latencyOk = checkLatency(tenantId);
  const endpoint = budgetOk && latencyOk ? getTenantEndpoint(tenantId) : getSharedEndpoint();
  return await predict(endpoint, req);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce per-tenant quotas in Feature Store and endpoints?
- How would you simulate rollback scenarios and validate audit trails?
